# Keyboard Shortcuts

## Architecture

Centralized registry in `shared/lib/shortcuts.ts`:

```
SHORTCUTS[]         ← catalog of all keyboard shortcuts (source of truth)
useShortcut()       ← React hook for registering a handler
formatShortcut()    ← "mod+k" → "⌘K" (macOS) / "Ctrl+K" (Windows/Linux)
getShortcutsByCategory() ← for help UI
```

## Usage

### Single shortcut

```tsx
import { useShortcut } from "~/shared/lib/shortcuts";

function SearchModal() {
  useShortcut("mod+k", () => setOpen(true), { context: "global" });
}
```

### Multiple in one component

```tsx
import { useShortcuts } from "~/shared/lib/shortcuts";

function ChatView() {
  useShortcuts([
    { combo: "escape", handler: () => cancel(), context: "chat" },
    { combo: "shift+n", handler: () => nextUnread(), context: "chat" },
    { combo: "mod+shift+m", handler: () => markAllRead(), context: "chat" },
  ]);
}
```

### Conditional

```tsx
useShortcut("arrowup", () => editLastMessage(), {
  context: "composer",
  enabled: inputIsEmpty,
});
```

## Shortcut Catalog

### Navigation

| Key | Action |
|-----|--------|
| `Mod+K` | Search |
| `Mod+1..4` | Messenger / Calendar / Mail / Calls |
| `Alt+↑/↓` | Previous / next chat (sidebar) |
| `Alt+←/→` | Back / Forward through history |
| `Mod+Shift+A` | My activity |
| Mouse 4/5 | Back / Forward (extra mouse buttons) |

### Message input (composer)

| Key | Action |
|-----|--------|
| `Enter` | Send |
| `Shift+Enter` | New line |
| `Escape` | Cancel editing |
| `↑` (when input is empty) | Edit last message |
| `Mod+B` | Bold |
| `Mod+I` | Italic |
| `Mod+Shift+X` | Strikethrough |
| `Mod+E` | Code (inline) |

### Chat

| Key | Action |
|-----|--------|
| `Escape` | Cancel selection / close panel |
| `Shift+N` | Next unread topic |
| `Mod+Shift+M` | Mark all as read |

### Interface

| Key | Action |
|-----|--------|
| `Mod+\` | Toggle sidebar |
| `Mod+.` | Toggle info panel |
| `Mod+/` | Keyboard shortcuts help |
| `Mod+Shift+T` | Toggle theme |

### Modal windows

| Key | Action |
|-----|--------|
| `Escape` | Close |

## Navigation History (back/forward)

The `shared/lib/navigation-history.ts` module provides history navigation:

```tsx
import { useNavigationHistory } from "~/shared/lib/navigation-history";

function NavBar() {
  const { goBack, goForward, canGoBack, canGoForward } = useNavigationHistory();

  return (
    <>
      <button disabled={!canGoBack} onClick={goBack}>←</button>
      <button disabled={!canGoForward} onClick={goForward}>→</button>
    </>
  );
}
```

### How it works

- Internal route stack (up to 100 entries, truncated to 80 on overflow)
- Works with both `BrowserRouter` (web/PWA) and `HashRouter` (Electron)
- `useSyncExternalStore` — reactively updates `canGoBack` / `canGoForward`
- Programmatic navigation (goBack/goForward) does not create duplicates in the stack

### Mouse buttons

`initMouseNavigation()` handles mouse button 3 (back) and button 4 (forward) — called once in the root component.

### Keyboard

`Alt+←` / `Alt+→` — standard shortcuts, registered in `SHORTCUTS[]`.

## Rules for AI Agent

### Adding a new keyboard shortcut

1. Add an entry to `SHORTCUTS[]` in `shared/lib/shortcuts.ts`
2. Use `useShortcut()` in the component
3. Always specify `context` — never register global shortcuts for screen-specific actions
4. `Mod` = `Cmd` on macOS, `Ctrl` on Windows/Linux — do not hardcode the platform

### Contexts

| Context | When active |
|---------|------------|
| `global` | Always (except modal) |
| `chat` | When a chat is open |
| `composer` | When focus is in the message input textarea |
| `sidebar` | When focus is in the sidebar |
| `modal` | When a modal window is open (blocks others) |

### Modal windows block shortcuts

When the DOM contains `[data-shortcut-context="modal"]`, all shortcuts except `modal` and `global` contexts are ignored. Add this attribute to modal overlays:

```tsx
<div data-shortcut-context="modal" className="...">
  {/* modal content */}
</div>
```

### Avoid conflicts

- `Mod+C/V/X/Z/A` — reserved by browser/OS
- `Mod+W/T/N` — reserved by browser (close/new tab)
- `Mod+L` — reserved by browser (address bar)
- `F1..F12` — reserved by OS/IDE
- `Mod+S` — do not use (no "save" in a messenger)

### Help overlay

To display the keyboard shortcuts help:

```tsx
import { getShortcutsByCategory, formatShortcut } from "~/shared/lib/shortcuts";

const categories = getShortcutsByCategory();
// Map<"Navigation", [{ key: "mod+k", label: "Search", ... }, ...]>
// formatShortcut("mod+k") → "⌘K" or "Ctrl+K"
```
